WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, fresh from the classic comics come Heroes in a Half Shell.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:29.640
Nostalgia And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.340
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.040
And I'm Joe.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.460
Guys, what can we really say about Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.260
What do you mean, Mike?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.380
Yeah, there's so much to say about Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.460
Are you stupid?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.100
I guess I'm a little stupid for asking two people that are very hostile, but I guess what

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.660
I mean is, is like, you know, Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, the NES game, is just like such

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.140
a small fraction of a gigantic franchise.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.480
Do we even bother like going into the nuance of all of this?

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.920
Do we just talk about the game?

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.440
What do you guys feel like talking about?

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.700
Joe, what do you feel like talking about when it comes to Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:17.060
I mean, I feel like talking about its relation to all its other games.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.780
Because I personally, as popular as Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles were, I was introduced to

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.160
it through the video games as a kid.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.940
This is one of the few games that I played growing up on the NES.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.120
Not too much, but I played a little bit.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.240
Oh, that's surprising to me.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.380
Sean, what would you say about the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles?

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:43.180
I'll say that all of my, you know, of all the bluster and hostility that I had earlier,

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.380
I don't really, like, I was never really into the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.300
Like, I played some of the, like, the beat-em-ups.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.800
That was really the top of my exposure to it growing up, though.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.880
I really, I can actually just leave if you want.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.280
No, no, no, it's fine.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.640
It's fine. Some people here are more acquainted with the Turtles than others.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:13.020
But it sounds like none of us really watched that first run on TV, the 1989 series that

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.960
it's, like, super popular for, the one that blasted it off into, you know, Turtle Mania.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.200
Is that true? I did not see that.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:25.520
You're correct. I mean, I probably, you know, it's one of those shows that maybe I had, like, caught

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.400
an episode of or two when I was a kid and I had nothing else to watch.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.160
But, yeah, I wasn't super into it.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.280
Although I do remember, you know, I remember one of my good friends and my neighbor would

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.920
always watch, um, would always watch the live-action movies.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.700
And I would watch those with him and I would like them, but I would also think, like, wow,

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.320
this is kind of weird. But I liked it.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:54.740
Weird how? You know, it bothered me that they were, like, just so obviously people in Turtles.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.760
Monsters? I don't know.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:01.800
Oh, okay. I feel like I just wanted them to, uh, just stick to animation until they were able to

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:07.660
make it look... I mean, look, knowing now as an adult what went into those costumes, I know how impressive

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.860
they were. But still, like, as a kid, I was just like, well, that looks fake.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.060
I'll wait until the PS4.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.980
Right, right. And it's funny, Joe, because you say, you know, like, you, you know, like, make them

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:24.620
wait. But then we did get the, uh, you know, the Michael Bay iteration of the Turtles.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:30.740
They're what you wish for. Some people might tell you that, you know, like, the costumes were better than the CGI.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.140
I'm sure they were.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.420
And I'm sure the plots of those movies were much better.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.500
I mean, I watched this when I was a kid.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.500
I don't really... All I remember was thinking, well, those are costumes.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.760
You know, it was my, you know, eight-year-old brain.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.260
Well, I've done a lot of work for Secret of the Ooze, actually, and that's the second

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.720
movie. And I can tell you, the amount of times I've seen that movie, uh, it's awful, actually.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.960
So, uh, I'm glad this game isn't based on Secret of the Ooze, which is really not even

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.640
a Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles movie.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:56.620
Can you say that?

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.440
Are you allowed to say, uh, to say that about that movie?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.780
I think so. I think I'm allowed to say not only...

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.400
Yeah, Mike, Mike, Mike. You love that movie.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.480
You tell me all the time how much you love that movie.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:10.240
Yep, yep. Uh, I love that movie so much, and the reason why I love it is because the turtles don't

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.320
fight at all in it.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.040
In fact, they, uh...

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:13.920
It's a character piece.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.500
Yeah, they don't even have weapons anymore.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:21.200
Yeah, I heard that, actually, that's the only Turtles movie where no two lightsabers touch.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:23.800
I don't understand.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:31.040
That could be true. Anyway, to get back to the point, uh, I was trying to get to the nice segue we had at

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.100
first, because we were talking about the 89 TV show.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:39.340
So, it's kind of interesting that the back of the box referenced the comics instead of

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:44.240
the TV show. I would think that the comics, having their limited run and everything, was more of a

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.080
niche thing that definitely, like, started the interest in the turtles, but that the

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.400
TV show on, you know, national television was the one that really, like, brought it up

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.560
to speed and made the, you know, they made the toys out of that and everything, and that

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.180
was the one that propelled it into the franchise it is today.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.060
But you'll notice that they're, they're definitely didn't make a mistake by calling out the comics,

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:10.500
because even on the box, the box art here, the turtles have, um, they're all wearing the

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.940
red masks. It's not, uh, you know, orange for Mikey and stuff like that.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:17.660
It's each one of them has the red mask, and that was something that was only done in the

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:22.140
comics. So, they were definitely saying, we're going for the comics here, not for the TV show.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.900
But, like, in the game, they have different colors.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.400
Yeah, but that's, like, again, like, that's something where I think, you know, it's almost

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:34.000
like two different design teams worked on this, right?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:38.320
Like, the box and the marketing was done by one section, and then the game was, like,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:41.780
probably, you know, updated along the way.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.820
We just have to, we're just going to have to keep, keep changing stuff.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.340
Well, because I don't think anything, I don't think anything in the game is based off the

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.940
comics. I don't think any of these were plot lines in the comics.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.800
You don't remember the fire people when they attacked?

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.860
Fire people are, those are real enemies.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:08.900
I imagine that, like, yeah, that, like, if the plan was to base it on the comics, somebody

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:13.340
somewhere down the line of production was like, hold on, we can't do that.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.800
This, people recognize now the, the TV show, we need to change it to that.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:23.260
Maybe there was some sort of, you know, some sort of miscommunication or something that

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.940
didn't line up between the creators or something.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:29.540
Yeah. And also, you know, Sean, just to go back to his name is Fire Freak.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.380
Oh, okay. You, you should know him very well, because he's an ex-pyromaniac from Brooklyn.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.620
He's, like, right up in your hood.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.860
Yeah. Well, I mean, I wasn't, I wasn't here yet, you know?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
Oh, okay. He doesn't, like, walk down the street occasionally and be like, I'm on fire.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:48.140
I'm on fire. No, he's, he definitely is probably moved out to the, like, the Hamptons or something.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:53.720
I'm sure all of our listeners assume whenever there's, you know, cop cars in the background

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.920
of our audio files that they're just reporting for Fire Freak.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.480
We won't talk about Fire Freak too much longer.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.800
Let's, let's get into the, into the game here for a second.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.660
This is a platforming game.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.640
I feel confident kind of saying that.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:14.260
It's a platforming adventure game, we'll add, where you play as the four Teenage Mutant Ninja

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:21.020
Turtles. You can switch at any time between Mikey, Raph, Leo, and Donnie, and you're traveling pretty

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:26.160
much through the, the city, but also, like, the sewers of the city and the warehouses

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.660
of the city. You're just basically traveling through New York City with the main goal to stop Shredder

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:35.800
and, and some other foes along the way, but stop Shredder from, what is it even that

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:36.920
he really is after?

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.920
Cause the whole thing is like, you gotta help.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:43.220
I think he's just like, yeah, he's just challenging you to come get it.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.260
Like, he's just like playing with us.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.300
It's like, Hey, I got Splinter.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.940
Like, you know, just try and get him.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:50.860
Yeah. He's the bad guy.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.660
He's, he's doing bad guy things.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.560
Yeah. But before we even get there, I mean, like, you know, it starts off with like almost a

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:58.560
mini episode.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:04.220
Yeah. You know, of like a larger plot where it's just like, you know, April has been kidnapped

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:05.780
by Bebop and Rocksteady.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.760
And now you have to go like save her.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.140
And that feels like it's going to be the whole game, right?

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.200
Like you, you get told that April's been kidnapped and now you're like, great, that's my mission.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.420
I gotta go like, you know, we're the four Marios and we got to save the princess.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.860
Yeah. It turns out to be like sort of a prologue.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:26.380
And from then on out, she says like, I'll provide support.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.340
And then she doesn't do anything.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:33.920
So you're really just on your own trying to find Shredder after that.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:38.420
Yeah. I thought I liked how they turned that trope on its head a little bit.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:42.820
Cause I used to always think that, you know, Final Fantasy was the first thing to do that,

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:46.780
to do the whole like, oh, go save the princess like every other video game.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:49.860
And then you get there and it's like, aha, there's a whole deeper plot here.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.020
And it turns out TMNT on the NES did it first.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.860
And, you know, even though that is just like a mini-sode, if you will,

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:05.620
or like just the prequel to the real game starting up, there's a lot of story in this game.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:12.000
And I don't know, I was a little surprised by how much storytelling they're doing in an early NES game like this.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.220
Did you guys think, I'm not saying like, did you think the story was complex or anything?

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:22.320
But like, was it cool that they actually tried to tell a story where you're traveling through New York City

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:25.060
and your mission kind of constantly evolves?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.260
I guess so.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.300
I mean, it seems to be more like just, they seem to be like episodes of a TV show.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.020
It's like, oh, well, here's the damn episode.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:37.480
And here's the Rescue April episode.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:44.260
And here's the, I'm driving a truck through the winding streets of Manhattan episode.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:50.180
And I didn't really see them as like a coherent or a cohesive whole.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:55.240
But yeah, at least there's like, there's different settings at least.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.040
The story is kind of, like you said, it just kind of reveals the next plot point.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:03.640
It's not, it's not this grand adventure or anything like that.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:04.980
You're just kind of moving along.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:07.600
You know, there's like the overworld map, right?

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:13.320
Where you see from like a top-down perspective, the turtles exploring the city or if they're not in the city,

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.040
wherever they happen to be next, like the dam or the secret headquarters.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:24.360
But then there's also like, where is the dam in the city?

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.780
Okay, where is the dam in New York City?

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:26.940
I want to know that too.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.220
But, you know, more importantly, I guess it's like, it's not, there's not levels, right?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.540
There's not like stage one, stage two.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:41.560
There are platforming portions of these, you know, whether they're the warehouses.

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:42.480
They're like dungeons.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:50.180
Yeah, they become a side-scrolling platforming game where you have to make it from one side to the other.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.340
But not all of them are necessary.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:56.020
Not everything that you have to, like there's no specific objectives necessarily.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.880
It's an interesting take on the platforming genre where they could have totally just done like,

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:08.440
here's stage one, you start in the sewers and your goal is to free April by the end of the level.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:14.980
You know, instead they really branch it out and try to make, you know, maybe unnecessary paths, but paths nonetheless.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.020
I thought that was a neat new approach.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:24.140
Yeah, I love the idea of, I love the idea of having this, like instead of an overworld map,

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:31.460
like Mario Brothers 3, Super Mario Brothers 3, having this like overworld world that you walk around on

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:38.760
and maybe there's, you know, maybe there's that little bit of like interaction with the overall world as you figure out,

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:45.060
oh, I should go to this, you know, the dam or I should go to this part of the sewer and do that level

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:48.780
because I want to get this item or I want to do this thing or like this should be the next part of my goal.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:54.540
I do think though that they, it's a cool idea, but they didn't execute it on it perfectly

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.420
because like you said, like it's a lot, I feel like there are a lot of dead ends

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.740
and there's a lot of times where you're just like, I guess I'll just go into another sewer

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.780
until I figure out which one's the right one.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:07.520
Like there's no, I feel like there wasn't enough to that whole overworld.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.900
I love the idea, but I wanted more from it.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:15.720
Yeah, it felt very much like a classic dungeon crawler where, you know,

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:22.240
you're going to find little dungeons to explore and they may have rewards,

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:28.100
like in some cases like a pizza or some shurikens,

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.840
but you also may just be wasting your time

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:37.440
and maybe that pizza is really just going to cover all the damage that you accrued just getting there.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:42.520
So, yeah, a lot of it was sort of like not necessary,

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:46.200
but I guess it does add to the scope of the game at least.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.660
Yeah, it feels like, you know, there's two thoughts to it.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.800
Either it was one of those things where it was intentional in order to inflate the game, right?

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:58.020
So that it takes longer and you're not really sure what you're doing

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.780
and you get to experience more and try new things.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:07.460
Or it could have been, you guys ever like go to those mini golf courses

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:12.360
where like the final hole usually has like a complex system of holes

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.260
where like you shoot it into one and then it goes down to another area.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:19.540
Like that's what this should have almost been is like theoretically,

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.840
any way, which way you go progresses you in the story.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:27.280
It's just that one might take you to like the more dangerous area

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.820
or another one might help you progress, like skip the next level

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.460
because you found the back entrance to the warehouse.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:38.700
I feel like that's what this game was actually like trying to do in some ways,

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.340
but instead you just get like what Sean was saying,

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:46.020
the prizes don't even really become prizes at a certain point

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:47.800
given how much it takes to get to them.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:54.820
Yeah, what you're describing sounds like telltale game design for adventure games,

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.320
but I think it works better in a system like this

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:01.680
where you may get a different gameplay experience,

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.560
but you're always moving forward.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.060
Yeah, or getting a good enough,

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.080
at least getting something that's like substantial enough of a bonus

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.260
that's not just another weapon that you could find in your regular levels anyways,

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.680
you know, for the ones that aren't moving you forward.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:21.420
All right, let's talk about the turtles,

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:25.500
which the manual wants you to know should not be confused with the beetles.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.900
I don't even think that's funny.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:33.700
I think it's funny, like it's so not funny and doesn't register that that makes it funny.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:36.140
Yeah, okay. Yeah, it's like now it's funny.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.380
So you got to laugh at a Sean.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.320
That was me. You know, but I guess like it could have, yeah,

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.020
not to be confused with like, you know,

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:45.320
the Italian Renaissance guys would have been like,

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.440
I guess more on the nose.

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.500
But so the turtles here, you know,

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:54.200
forget about the switching mechanic for a minute

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.080
because I feel like that's a whole different thing.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.500
I just want to talk about what it feels like to control the turtles

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:02.740
because there's not much changing between the four of them.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:05.740
So if you just think about platformers we've played

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:10.660
or even like more adventurous style games that are side scrollers, right?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.320
In these kinds of games that we played,

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:18.400
I feel like the first thing I noticed right away is you usually don't get a sprite this large

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.360
as your character.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:25.960
These are some of the largest sprites I've ever seen for a platformer.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:31.380
And I think that's like, that's where my problems kind of start is

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:38.340
in some ways the worst part of this game is just what it feels like to be the turtles.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:42.060
They're always in these claustrophobic environments

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:45.880
where they can jump so high but it doesn't matter, right?

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.200
Or they can, you know, like they can reach things

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.600
that don't necessarily need to be reached.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.280
And they just like feel like they're bonking their heads

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:58.300
or they're walking into enemies that it's just not necessary.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:01.440
I almost wonder if this game,

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:06.200
if they had the turtles just the size of or the smoothness

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.660
of a Mario or even a Mega Man, right?

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:11.960
Mega Man would probably be more on point with the different power-ups

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:12.780
that the turtles have.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:16.520
Just if they had that kind of layout to them,

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:21.100
would this have been more fun for the side-scrolling perspective of it

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.840
instead of having to do the chore of just,

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.020
I don't want to say even just the movement in general,

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.540
but like being these characters,

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:34.180
I didn't feel particularly strong or dominating

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.800
or even like a Ninja Turtle really.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.680
I just felt like I was a guy on his way.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.640
Yeah, this feels like,

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:44.720
okay, so developing a Ninja Turtles game

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.640
with the control scheme that it has

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:50.160
and the actions that you can perform

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:55.160
to me feels like developing a Batman game

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.740
with like Resident Evil style tank controls.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:03.040
Like it just isn't conducive to like the kind of property

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.460
that they're developing for

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:09.520
and they already have like the beat-em-up genre,

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:14.580
at least the early iterations of it

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.040
to like sort of draw from.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.700
They just didn't think to do that.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:22.640
So instead we get this really weird combination.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:26.040
I didn't know that the Turtles could jump like three stories.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.920
I didn't know that that was a thing that they did.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.900
If the game property,

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.960
if the Ninja Turtles are about martial arts

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.980
and different melee weapons,

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:37.380
I feel like they should have put a little bit more

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.300
into making that feel good

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.560
instead of like just press the button

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.520
and that's all we got.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.700
Yeah, I totally agree.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:46.920
I feel like the whole,

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.380
the whole point of this is to feel like a ninja

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.900
and that doesn't happen when everything kind of feels

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.440
like you're trudging through mud the whole time.

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:58.420
You know, everything feels, we've had other games that feel this way too,

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:01.480
but it's, but, but they're not always necessarily as bad

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.880
because you're not, you're not expecting to feel fast

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:04.720
and to feel nimble.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.000
Um, you know,

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.480
I will say as far as the sprite size,

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:10.700
I feel like we have had other games

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:13.040
that like have this, like even Castlevania or,

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:14.240
or like Metroid,

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:16.320
don't they feel kind of like it's the same size sprite,

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.520
but something about those games.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:18.800
Oh, that's a good point. Yeah, you're right. Metroid,

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.280
Metroid is a good example there.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:23.040
Yeah. But something about those games feel a little better,

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.280
you know? Yeah, the level design.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.740
you're, you're, you're primary,

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:26.980
oh yeah, but Metroid,

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:28.040
you're primarily using,

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.100
like firing a weapon,

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.540
you know, like a projectile

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.260
rather than using like melee

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:33.560
and while there's projectiles in here too,

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:34.480
just something about it feels

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.860
so much slower.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:38.700
Everything feels, I mean,

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:39.900
the best way I can put it is like, yeah,

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.640
like you're trudging through mud

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.640
to do it. Yeah, definitely.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.060
And you got to keep in mind,

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.520
we have a great ninja game

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:47.820
on the NES. We,

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.440
we put it on the essential games list,

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.900
it's Ninja Gaiden, and the way Ryu controls in that game

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.100
is, is just really cool.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.740
Like he's always moving fast.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.520
He, his melee attacks,

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:01.460
while not being like incredibly varied,

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:03.100
I mean, it's the NES, but like his melee attacks,

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:03.920
they feel good

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.720
to make contact with the enemies.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.660
I think somewhere between

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:12.160
the way, the slowness of the turtles

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.440
and just the way

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:14.840
that their weapons behave

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.520
is the two things

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:17.800
that just immediately to me,

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.360
it's like, I'm convinced I'm playing

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.340
a turtles game. I,

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:22.460
you know, like everything about the story

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.260
and the look of the turtles

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.520
and, and the environments,

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.000
like I'm all for it,

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:29.240
right? I'm, I'm believing it,

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.780
but I don't feel like

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:31.700
I'm a Ninja Turtle

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.080
when I'm playing this game

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.580
and even when you switch

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:35.880
between the turtles,

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.100
which is just something that

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.260
is done pretty clever

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:39.140
where you just like,

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.760
similar to Mega Man's powers

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:41.960
changing between screens,

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:42.980
you just pause,

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.540
select which turtle you want

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.860
and it's an immediate swap in.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:46.960
What a chore it would be

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.260
if you had to go to like

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.160
the base

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.620
or, or a nearby area

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.800
to swap between turtles.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.220
It's great that you can swap them

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:55.560
on the fly, but it really doesn't mean much

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.800
unless you,

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:58.720
uh, unless you chose Raph,

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.220
in which case, you know,

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.360
your, your weapon sucks.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:02.840
So now you're basically like,

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.400
you know, you have even less range,

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.240
like at least with the other guys,

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.180
they have a little, you know,

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.760
they have, they have good range on their stuff,

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:11.300
but they still don't do enough special.

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:13.560
Like I would think Donnie's bow

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.300
would be a lot different

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.700
than what, you know,

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.880
um, Leo could do with the,

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:21.340
the Katana. Like something about that.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.760
It just, it doesn't feel right

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.100
that they're basically just like,

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.680
Oh, the lengths at which they attack

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:27.780
are different. Yeah.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.700
It should be, it should be cool stuff

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.240
that makes each turtle feel unique.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.600
Well, you know what?

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.920
Like between, between the fighting,

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:36.540
not being all that great

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.880
and the trudging through mud,

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.000
it seems like the developers of this game

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.560
went more turtle

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.500
than they went ninja.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.200
Sean, go back to your show.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.200
And then what's funny about,

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:56.240
what's funny about this whole,

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.520
like, since we're talking about the combat

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.900
for a minute, um,

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.260
the, the forget that like,

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.140
you know, the Katana,

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.200
the bow, the nunchucks,

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.360
which again, like the nunchucks,

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:06.520
the nunchucks, what a cool opportunity

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:07.840
to do something interesting,

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:09.900
um, for Michelangelo there

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:11.440
where like, you know, maybe he could,

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.580
I don't know, spin them around

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.800
and, and do a little,

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.240
give him like some kind of,

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.400
give him some hover ability

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:18.280
for a second, right?

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.100
If he can, if he can spin them fast enough,

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.740
I don't know. But the,

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:23.940
the other power-ups

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.400
in this game are like,

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:27.100
I don't know, they're not like

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.000
the boomerang,

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.980
for example, right? Not necessarily something

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:31.300
I associate the Ninja Turtles

